<PageLayout description="Matt McManus works in quantitative trading and prediction markets at DRW.">
  <p>
    I work on prediction markets at <a href="https://drw.com/">DRW</a>, where I
    research and trade systematic strategies in event-driven markets.
  </p>

  <p>
    Previously, I worked in quantitative research and machine learning at
    <a href="https://www.twosigma.com/">Two Sigma</a> and
    <a href="https://www.bridgewater.com/">Bridgewater Associates</a>. I received
    my B.S. and M.Eng. from MIT in computer science and mathematics, where my
    research included scientific machine learning, neural differential equations,
    and AI systems.
  </p>

  <p>
    I also previously led <a href="https://pokerbots.org/">MIT Pokerbots</a>, an
    autonomous poker competition focused on game theory and algorithmic
    decision-making.
  </p>

  <hr />

  <p class="interests">
    <strong>Interests:</strong> Quantitative trading, prediction markets, market
    microstructure, probabilistic forecasting, and machine learning.
  </p>
